  "description": "POV: you buy snacks at the movies. Follow your snack dollar to AMC's books.\n\nSources:\n- AMC Entertainment Holdings: Form 8-K with Q4 and full-year 2025 earnings release (Feb 23, 2026): https://investor.amctheatres.com/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001411579-26-000018/0001411579-26-000018.pdf\n\nFrom the cited page: for the year ended Dec 31, 2025, AMC food and beverage revenues were $1,671.3 million and food and beverage costs were $327.0 million; U.S. food and beverage revenue per patron was $8.57; consolidated average ticket price was $12.09; consolidated attendance was 219,412 thousand. Our math: 327.0 / 1,671.3 = 19.6%, so 19.6 cents of each snack dollar is cost and 80.4 cents is left before other expenses such as rent and pay; 1,671.3 - 327.0 = $1,344.3 million; 1,344.3 / 12.09 = about 111 million tickets, about half of 219.4 million guests. Costs shown are only the cost of the snacks themselves. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #amc #movies #howtheymakemoney",
